---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { relationTypes } from '../lib/data';
---

<Layout title="About">
  <div class="wrap prose">
    <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span aria-current="page">About</span>
    </nav>
    <h1>
      Built on the
      <br />
      work of <em>many.</em>
    </h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Behind a familiar piece of software is a collection of ideas, tools and decisions. Shoulders
      is a small invitation to look closer.
    </p>
    <h2>What did its creators add?</h2>
    <p>
      A runtime does not give you a finished editor. A database does not give you an operated
      backend. A video encoder does not give you a production desk. Bringing those parts together
      takes engineering, judgment and care.
    </p>
    <p>
      Each exploration gives that work a place alongside the foundations. You can discover the
      component, understand its specific role, and find out what using it independently would
      involve.
    </p>
    <h2 id="method">A few connections, carefully chosen.</h2>
    <p>
      This edition covers VS Code, Supabase, OBS Studio, Firefox, Blender and Godot. Every
      connection includes primary sources, a verification date and a scope. An upstream source
      snapshot does not establish what is installed on your machine or every component in a managed
      deployment.
    </p>
    <p>
      The architectural plates illustrate the idea of supporting foundations. Their geometry is not
      a dependency graph. A deeper connection appears only when a source supports it.
    </p>
    <h2>From software to physical resources.</h2>
    <p>
      Deeper trails distinguish a documented software integration from a selected operating-system
      example and a general physical foundation. A Linux path does not identify the host behind a
      managed service. A silicon or electricity connection does not identify its supplier.
    </p>
    <p>
      Materials and energy are separate branches. We do not turn a published retail price into a
      production cost, or infer a utility, power mix or consumption figure from a dependency.
    </p>
    <h2>Words that keep the edges clear.</h2>
    <dl>
      {Object.entries(relationTypes).map(([type, meaning]) => (
        <>
          <dt>{type[0].toUpperCase() + type.slice(1)}</dt>
          <dd>{meaning}</dd>
        </>
      ))}
    </dl>
    <p>
      None of these relationships establishes payment or endorsement. The curated dataset is
      intentionally small: an absent connection means we have not documented it here.
    </p>
    <h2>Help choose the next exploration.</h2>
    <p>
      Have a particular product or foundation in mind? Send its name and, if you have one, a source
      we should read.
    </p>
    <a class="text-link" href="/request/">
      Suggest an exploration →
    </a>
  </div>
</Layout>
